  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the dominant driver of performance (config_007: 0.7062 vs config_020: 0.6352 with pca_n2000), and the image modality adds ~5.6 pts on top of the RNA-only scvi_n200 baseline (config_040: 0.6501). However, we have only tested one image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) with scvi_n200. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the image contribution is encoder-specific or whether a lighter backbone like resnet50 captures comparable signal. This experiment (config_014: scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) is a clean single-variable change from the best-performing config_007, isolating the image encoder effect while holding the RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion, and profile setting at their known-best values. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it either confirms imagenet_vit_l is necessary (justifying its compute cost) or reveals that resnet50 is sufficient (freeing the search to focus on other dimensions), and it directly informs whether the ~5.6-pt image gain is robust to encoder choice."
